 "slug": "3-4-derivatives-as-rates-of-change",
 "title": "Derivatives as Rates of Change",
 "content": "<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><body><div data-type=\"page\" id=\"page_610ace30-270f-4dfc-8fad-5e44c4723919\" class=\"chapter-content-module\" data-book-content=\"true\"><h2 data-type=\"document-title\" id=\"page_610ace30-270f-4dfc-8fad-5e44c4723919_titlecreatedbycookbook\" data-rex-keep=\"true\"><span class=\"os-number\">3.4</span>\n<span class=\"os-divider\"> </span>\n<span data-type=\"\" itemprop=\"\" class=\"os-text\">Derivatives as Rates of Change</span>\n</h2><p id=\"fs-id1169739305060\">Next, use <span class=\"os-math-in-para\"><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> to approximate <span class=\"os-math-in-para\"><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>101</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> the revenue obtained from the sale of the 101st dinner. Since <span class=\"os-math-in-para\"><math display=\"inline\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow></semantics></math></span> the revenue obtained from the sale of the 101st dinner is approximately $3.</p>\n</div></body></html>"
}